config BR2_PACKAGE_TUSB926X_FLASH_BURNER
	bool "tusb926x-flash-burner"
	depends on BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUSB
	help
	  In-circuit flash programmer for the TI TUSB9260/TUSB9261
	  USB 3.0 to SATA bridge.

	  The bridge has no application flash of its own: its boot code
	  loads an image from the attached SPI flash into RAM, and with
	  no valid image it idles in a HID boot loader.  This tool talks
	  to that boot loader and writes the image, so the bridge can be
	  programmed without desoldering the SPI flash.

	  On the NMS-SM-K1892VM21YA the SPI flash (D15) is wired to
	  nothing but the bridge, and the bridge sits on downstream port
	  1 of the TUSB8041 hub, which is not brought out to the SMARC
	  connector.  The SoC is therefore the only host that can reach
	  it, and this tool has to run on the module itself.

	  Local patch 0001 talks to /dev/hidraw directly instead of
	  going through hidapi, so no udev is required.

	  https://github.com/luxonis/tusb926x-flash-burner
